course: dictionary
lesson: 10634
title: Unhappy and its shades
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Unhappy is made of two parts: un- means not, and happy means glad or cheerful. So unhappy means not happy. «A bored pet can become unhappy and destructive» tells us the pet feels sad and fed up when it has nothing to do.
explain: The word can also mean not pleased with something. Look at the words after it: with, about or at tell you what the feeling is aimed at. «She was unhappy with her mark» means she did not like her mark.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping in "not happy" and checking that the sentence still makes sense. «The teacher thought she was unhappy at school» works with "not happy at school", so you have the right meaning.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means not, so unhappy means not happy.
fact: «Unhappy» is an adjective, and its noun form is unhappiness.
fact: Its comparison forms are unhappier and unhappiest, or more unhappy and most unhappy.
fact: «Glum, sad, miserable and heartbroken all mean unhappy, but each a different amount.» Heartbroken is the strongest of these.
fact: If you feel unhappy for a long time, tell a trusted adult. Asking for help is a brave and sensible thing to do.
exercise: In «A bored pet can become unhappy and destructive», what does unhappy mean? | *Sad and fed up | Quick and clever | Very hungry | Loud and noisy
exercise: «The teacher thought she was unhappy at school.» What does unhappy at suggest? | Too tired to walk to school | Excited to go to school | *Not happy with school, feeling sad about it | Lost on the way to school
exercise: Find the noun form of unhappy. | unhappen | unhappier | unhappily | *unhappiness
test: Which word is the comparative of unhappy, meaning more unhappy? | unhappiness | most unhappy | *unhappier | unhappyer
test: In «Paying a frenemy back with the same unkindness usually makes two frenemies and two unhappy people», what does unhappy mean? | Very tall | *Sad and hurt | Quiet and calm | Lucky
exam: Which sentence uses unhappy to mean not satisfied? | The sun was shining over the park | The dog ran to fetch the ball | We ate lunch by the river | *She was unhappy with her mark
